  "description": "3.0.0\n      - Depends on Carbon.MassTransit [3.11.0,4.0.0) and MassTransit [7.3.1,8.0.0) (MassTransit 7) as package\n        references, so services on MassTransit 7 can use Carbon.WebApplication 6.x. Services on MassTransit 8\n        should stay on Carbon.Audit 2.0.0; they get NU1608 at restore, and with \"CarbonAudit:Enabled\" true\n        AddCarbonAudit throws an InvalidOperationException naming the mismatch.\n      - A direct reference to Carbon.Audit 2.0.0 or to Carbon.MassTransit below 3.11.0 becomes an NU1605\n        downgrade error; raise it (Carbon.MassTransit 3.11.0) or remove it.\n      2.0.0\n      - MassTransit upgraded to 8.5.8 together with Carbon.MassTransit 4.0.0 (BREAKING: MassTransit 8).\n      1.5.0\n      - DbContextOptionsBuilder.AddCarbonAuditInterceptor(serviceProvider) added.\n      - AuditInterceptor no longer collects events for saves outside an HTTP request (seeding, Quartz jobs,\n        consumers); those were never published.\n      - AuditInterceptor also intercepts synchronous SaveChanges().\n      - RequestContext and AuditInterceptor are always registered; the interceptor is inert when disabled.\n      - CarbonAuditSettings bound from \"CarbonAudit\"; UseCarbonAudit() is a no-op when disabled.\n      - The audit bus and IAuditEventPublisher are registered only when enabled.\n      1.4.0\n      - .NET 10 (net10.0) target framework added.\n      1.3.0\n      - ApiStatusCode, ErrorCode, Messages and DurationMs added to audit events; HttpStatusCodeFilter added.\n      1.2.0\n      - Carbon.MassTransit dependency and Carbon.Audit's own MassTransit implementation added.\n      1.1.1\n      - Token header treated as sensitive and redacted.\n      1.1.0\n      - Dedicated HTTP request audit event publishing added.\n      1.0.2\n      - TransactionId accepted as CorrelationId fallback; FailedRequest event (AuditAction.FailedRequest = 3)\n        for HTTP >= 400 without DB changes; events emitted for every outcome; HttpStatusCode added.\n      1.0.1\n      - Advanced audit filtering options added.\n      1.0.0\n      - Initial release. RequestContextMiddleware, AuditInterceptor and audit constants added.",
  "id": "Carbon.Audit",
